  N19_Idempotency [label="IDEMPOTENCY CHECKS BEFORE OUTPUT
================================
Before writing or applying:
- check whether equivalent closeout already exists
- check whether intended target row/function/variable/plan entry already exists
- if equivalent state exists, prefer no-op with evidence over rewriting
- if path exists and ALLOW_OVERWRITE=no, write versioned artifact or stop
- no duplicate TSV rows
- no duplicate package tokens
- no duplicate bootstrap step names
- no duplicate allowlist entries
- no duplicate profile plan entries
- no silent function replacement
- no unmanaged target env edits that break managed block ownership/mode

Same manifest + same live state + same plan should produce the same application decision and no duplicate edits.", color="#F9A825", fillcolor="#FFFDE7"];
  N20_Safety [label="SAFE COMMANDS / FORBIDDEN ACTIONS
=================================
Allowed in CIP06 only after confirmation:
- read approved manifest/snapshot/plan
- inspect exact target files
- apply exact approved low-risk patches
- generate Codex pack when direct apply is not allowed
- run syntax/read-only validation commands
- run one exact managed step only if explicitly approved
- produce closeout, evidence, snapshot/export artifacts

Forbidden unless explicitly manifest-approved and user-confirmed:
- config mutation
- public tooling edit
- DOT mutation
- evidence mutation beyond closeout output
- package installation
- env creation
- bootstrap step execution
- mount/pull/push
- credential read/print
- Docker/Runpod/paid APIs/live infra
- destructive account lifecycle
- broad directory mutation
- prior companion mutation

Always forbidden:
- printing secrets
- relying on active shell Python instead of explicit target env policy
- broad bootstrap for validation
- claiming success without validation evidence.", color="#BF360C", fillcolor="#FBE9E7"];
  N21_ResponseFormat [label="REQUIRED RESPONSE FORMAT
========================
Current phase: CIP06 idempotent application + closeout
Selected DOT:
Addressed role:
Variable block proposed/confirmed:
Approval chain status:
Manifest items selected:
Config state snapshot used:
Integration plan used:
Application mode:
Patch classes:
Exact files to read:
Exact files to create/modify:
Forbidden surfaces preserved:
Idempotency strategy:
Validation plan:
Post-config smoke plan:
Closeout artifacts planned/created:
Snapshot/export planned/created:
Safety status:
Decision: PASS / STOP / BLOCKED / NO-OP / DELEGATED
Recommended next route:", color="#37474F", fillcolor="#ECEFF1"];
  N22_PassStop [label="PASS / STOP CONDITIONS
======================
PASS only if:
- variables confirmed
- required source contract applied or missing-source fallback explicitly approved
- manifest approval chain verified
- CIP04 snapshot and CIP05 plan are present and consistent
- application mode selected
- exact file touch set confirmed
- idempotency checks performed
- only approved patch classes applied or delegated
- validation/postcheck artifacts produced
- evidence/snapshot/closeout obligations satisfied
- no forbidden mutation occurred.

STOP if:
- user has not confirmed
- manifest approval is absent or ambiguous
- CIP04 live-state snapshot is missing/stale for the planned surface
- CIP05 plan is missing or conflicts with manifest/snapshot
- target files are broad/unknown
- patch class is high-risk and lacks explicit approval
- credential/live/destructive action appears
- overwrite would occur with ALLOW_OVERWRITE=no
- validation plan is missing
- implementation would require public/DOT/config mutation not allowed by variables.

After PASS:
Do not silently start another CIP phase. Recommend the next route based on result.", color="#B71C1C", fillcolor="#FFEBEE"];
  N23_Reentry [label="RE-ENTRY INTO CIP AND V7 PIPELINE
=================================
If result is NO-OP:
- preserve closeout evidence and return to operator.

If result is DELEGATED:
- run the produced Codex implementation pack in the real workspace.

If result is BLOCKED:
- return to CIP03 or human design to revise manifest approval.

If result requires updated live truth:
- rerun CIP04.

If result requires replanning:
- rerun CIP05.

If config contract was changed:
- create/update evidence snapshot/export.
- prepare companion/update-note inputs.
- consider 0C extraction note if repeated manual work suggests deterministic tooling.

CIP06 completes the config-infra integration loop for an approved item. It does not replace normal skeleton/organ P lanes; it applies their approved config-infra handoff later and safely.", color="#333333", fillcolor="#F5F5F5"];
